{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.AdditiveSignChangingTerm","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MassTheory.AdditiveSignChangingTerm","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.fit_hits_physical_residuals","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.fit_hits_physical_residuals","kind":"theorem","line":134,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/AdditiveSignChangingTerm.lean#L134-L141","doc":"**(V″) Concrete instance at the physical residuals.**  The #4307 target pair\n`(m₃, m₄) = (0.4708, −2.7080)` is hit by the two-weight fit — witnessing that the\nmagnitude match is *guaranteed*, hence non-evidential.  (The values `0.4708`,\n`−2.7080` enter ONLY as an arbitrary target of the surjective map; nothing is\nsolved *from* them into a canonical structural weight.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.fit_is_unique","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.fit_is_unique","kind":"theorem","line":123,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/AdditiveSignChangingTerm.lean#L123-L132","doc":"**(V′) Uniqueness — the fit is fully determined, i.e. it has NO residual\nfreedom.**  Two weight pairs producing the same `(M(3), M(4))` are equal.  With\n(V) this says the two-weight form is a *bijection* onto residual pairs: 2 free\nparameters, 2 constraints, exactly one solution.  Reproducing the physical\nresiduals `(+0.4708, −2.7080)` consumes both degrees of freedom and predicts\nnothing — the anti-fit certificate. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.fit_hits_any_target","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.fit_hits_any_target","kind":"theorem","line":110,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/AdditiveSignChangingTerm.lean#L110-L121","doc":"**(V) Anti-fit identifiability — the two-weight map is a linear isomorphism.**\nThe map `(s, t) ↦ (3s − t, 6s − 4t)` sending the (edge, triangle) weights to the\n`(M(3), M(4))` residual pair is **surjective**: for *any* target `(m₃, m₄)` there\nexist weights reproducing it — explicitly `s = (2/3)(m₃ − m₄/4)·(3/2)`… (the closed\ninverse below).  Because the target is always hit, matching both residuals is\n**guaranteed** and carries no predictive content.\n\nThe witnesses are the exact inverse of the `det = −6` system:\n`s = (4·m₃ − m₄)/6`, `t = (6·m₃ − 3·m₄)/6 = m₃ − m₄/2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.signChange_iff_window","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.signChange_iff_window","kind":"theorem","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/AdditiveSignChangingTerm.lean#L99-L108","doc":"**(W) The sign-change window is exactly `(3/2, 3)`** — a parameter-free\nstructural characterisation.  The bond−frustration additive term reproduces the\n#4307 sign pattern (`+` at A=3, `−` at A=4) **iff** the frustration weight\n`κ ∈ (3/2, 3)`.  The *sign* the data requires is thus derived from the simplex\nbond/face counts, with no appeal to the residual magnitudes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.window_gives_signChange","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.window_gives_signChange","kind":"theorem","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/AdditiveSignChangingTerm.lean#L85-L97","doc":"**(W←) Any `κ ∈ (3/2, 3)` realises the sign change.**  For `s > 0` and\n`3/2 < κ < 3`, the term is positive at A=3 and negative at A=4 — the #4307 sign\npattern.  So the bond−frustration mechanism is structurally *capable* of the\nrequired sign change on the whole open interval `(3/2, 3)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.signChange_forces_window","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.signChange_forces_window","kind":"theorem","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/AdditiveSignChangingTerm.lean#L66-L83","doc":"**(W→) Sign change forces `κ ∈ (3/2, 3)`.**  If the (positively-scaled,\n`s > 0`) bond−frustration term is `> 0` at A=3 and `< 0` at A=4, then the\nfrustration-per-triangle weight lies strictly in `(3/2, 3)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.bondFrustA4","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.bondFrustA4","kind":"def","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/AdditiveSignChangingTerm.lean#L63-L64","doc":"The bond−frustration simplex term at A=4: `M(4)/s = C(4,2) − κ·C(4,3) = 6 − 4κ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.bondFrustA3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.bondFrustA3","kind":"def","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/AdditiveSignChangingTerm.lean#L60-L61","doc":"The bond−frustration simplex term at A=3: `M(3)/s = C(3,2) − κ·C(3,3) = 3 − κ`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}